<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4570"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lanena<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lanena<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 6:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Okay-so there was semen found at the Nancy Fox scene and the Oteros for sure and maybe Shirley Vian?  I am confused...why is this not known?  I mean if there really is sufficient DNA and if it is still testable, why can&#39;t we &#40;public&#41; know which scenes it was recoverd from?  It is not like he can change his DNA type or something.  I only ask again and press this question because  <BR>I have heard that maybe the DNA is no longer testable because it was stored incorrectly and therefore the WPD has nothing.  SO my questions are... <BR>1&#41; How can it be known for sure what scenes semen was found at? <BR>2&#41; Why do you think this is such a secret in the eyes of the WPD if they really have DNA? <BR>Thanks<!--/Text--></td></tr>
