<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4606"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 8:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom, <BR> <BR>I enjoyed seeing the pictures of your trip. One that I do not enjoy seeing is the photo of Shirley Vian&#39;s gravesite, although I am glad you posted it for everyone, including BTK, to see. It&#39;s a sobering visceral reminder to all of us that we&#39;re trying to unmask someone who has seen to it that at least 8 human beings will never know life on this earth again. And as for BTK, perhaps seeing it will inspire some remorse. I doubt it, but hope springs eternal, doesn&#39;t it?  <BR> <BR>Are you at liberty to tell the rest of us about the ice trays?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
