<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4676"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 7:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy, I agree, I don&#39;t necessarily think this is a WPD cover-up, but it does introduce another tangent.  Why would the officer admit to this if he was the perpetrator?  BTW, I like your undeducated theory post, it describes someone I know here in Wichita in ways that are scary.  Maybe I&#39;ll start keeping an eye on him more!  So, this isn&#39;t the place to talk about that though.  We are talkin to Tom here.  So Tom, are you satisfied with the Wichita media coverage of your site?  Are you looking into conducting more interviews?  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4676-->
