<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4700"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 1:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Tom <BR> <BR>Do you know if this statment of Tippu´s is a fact? <BR> <BR>&#34;The ice tray evidence was becoming of more considerable importance, when after almost two weeks into the investigation, a Sheriff’s deputy &#40;could have been a detective&#41; admitted that he had helped himself to some ice tea from the victim&#39;s refrigerator, and had forgotten to replace the ice trays. As he was a first responder, the trays were taken out before the crime scene photographer&#39;s photo shoot, and therefore the ice trays were in the pics. How does that factual kool-aid add to the mix of &#34;WPD cover-up theories&#34;?????? Very interesting...could it have been the same person that &#34;accidentally&#34; stepped in the blood and left the boot print? &#34; <BR> <BR>And if so, do you know what happened to that cop? I just can´t belive it, that a cop in a crimesceene with four people murdered in the most horrific way, two of them children, going into the victims refrigerator and drink their icetea!!! and on top of it providing himself with icecubs. It sounds just unbeliveble to me. <BR> <BR>Another thing I would like to ask you is: <BR>Is it true that there was a psychic present with a cop all night in the Oteros house the first night after the murder? and if so, WHY  was the psychic there? I mean as far as I know, police dont work with psychicks unless their case is going cold ect. And where did that psychic come from? so what is the facts about this info, do you know? <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
